  "details": "Hi, so I, as many of vrchat players, can't affort a motion controller, at least yet. So something came to mind. Why don't the developers make it possible to move the arms/hands with your mouse? I would work similar to other games, here's my idea:\n\nHOLD left click: Enables movement of left arm+hand.\nHOLD right click: Enables movement of right arm+hand\nHOLD E: Grab/activate objects (like pen)\nPRESS/HOLD Q: drop/throw objects\nCTRL + ALT: Rotation of hand.\nOthers: fingers's\nEXTRA: A key to freeze player's camera, to better controll of the arm (on a non-vr user)\n\nVRchat have alot of unbinded keys that could be use on keyboards, to people who can't affot a motion controller's set, that would make interaction's between player alot more fun. \n\nOf course it would have some limitations, like you can't use both arms at the same time in different directions, but still, it would be a big upgrade.\n\nI think that's it, any ideas how to improve this method, please feel free to talk :)",
